        "+3V3",
        "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)",
        "unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)",
        "Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)"
      ],
      "observed": "The LDO output net +3.3V is connected to sensors and other peripherals, but the separate +3V3 net containing FCC1/NAVC1 VBAT and pull-ups has no source from REG2. All FCC1 and NAVC1 VDD pins are on unconnected nets, and NAVC1 VSS pins are only tied together on Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18), not to GND.",
      "expected": "The specification states that the 3.3 V LDO feeds both MCUs and sensors. STM32 VDD pins must be connected to the 3.3 V supply and VSS pins to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "From these two regulated rails, 3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"92\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCUs are not powered from the regulated 3.3 V rail; NAVC1 also lacks a connection to board GND. This would prevent the flight controller from operating.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": [
        "FCC1",
        "UART3_FCC1"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "FCC1.48",
        "FCC1.73",
        "UART3_FCC1.3",
        "UART3_FCC1.4"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "UART3_TX_FCC",
        "UART3_RX_FCC"
      ],
      "observed": "FCC1 pin 48, named VCAP and typed power_out, is on UART3_TX_FCC together with UART3_FCC1 pin 3. FCC1 pin 73, also VCAP/power_out, is on UART3_RX_FCC together with UART3_FCC1 pin 4.",
      "expected": "VCAP pins are internal regulator decoupling pins and should connect only to decoupling capacitors to GND. UART3 TX/RX should use alternate-function GPIO pins, not VCAP power pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"146\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC internal regulator VCAP nodes are shorted to an external UART connector, likely preventing proper regulator start-up and potentially damaging the MCU or corrupting UART3.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": [
        "HSE1",
        "HSE2",
        "FCC1",
        "NAVC1"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "FCC1.5",
        "FCC1.37",
        "FCC1.12",
        "FCC1.13",
        "NAVC1.5",
        "NAVC1.6",
        "HSE1.1",
        "HSE1.3",
        "HSE2.1",
        "HSE2.3"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "HSE_IN_FCC",
        "HSE_OUT_FCC",
        "Net-(FCC1-PH0)",
        "VREF+_FCC",
        "HSE_IN_NAVC",
        "HSE_OUT_NAVC",
        "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)",
        "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"
      ],
      "observed": "The FCC HSE crystal is connected to FCC1 pins 5 and 37, which are PE6 and PE7, while the oscillator pins PH0 and PH1 are on Net-(FCC1-PH0) and VREF+_FCC with capacitors only. The NAVC HSE crystal nets HSE_IN_NAVC and HSE_OUT_NAVC contain HSE2, load capacitors, and a series resistor but no NAVC1 pin; NAVC1 PH0/PH1 are connected only to 2.2 uF capacitors.",
      "expected": "The specification states that both MCUs use an ABM8G 25 MHz HSE crystal. For STM32H753VITx and STM32F405RGTx, the HSE crystal should be connected to the OSC_IN/OSC_OUT pins, PH0/PH1 in these LQFP packages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The intended external high-speed clock is not connected to the MCU oscillator pins, so the MCUs would not receive the specified HSE clock and the design would not operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show multiple serious deviations from the intended HadesFCS design, most notably that the MCU power/ground connections are open and the 3.3 V rail is split, plus VCAP pins are shorted to UART3 and the HSE crystals are not connected to the MCU oscillator pins."
}

